  "hypothesis": "Selective reversible PIK3C2B inhibition improves established human MTM1-deficient contractile dysfunction across relevant genotypes at measured free tissue exposures preserving neural and hepatobiliary function.",
  "changes_vs_round4": [
    "Integrated endogenous MTM1-C375S catalytic-loss model and reconciled local protein rescue.",
    "Separated juvenile genetic rescue, acute fiber physiology and exact-drug delayed treatment.",
    "Elevated AZD8055 to a bounded functional comparator; audited bias and label limitations.",
    "Added 2026 diet-sensitized liver biology and large-animal safety-prediction failure.",
    "Verified current ASP2957 registry state without assuming efficacy.",
    "Added female/genotype and secondary immune-function boundaries."
  ],
